          "title": "Solvable Sokoban Without a Solver via Diffusion",
          "title_zh": "无需求解器：基于扩散模型的可解 Sokoban 生成",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15958v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_top",
          "organization": "DeepMind",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.15958",
          "summary": "A transformer-based discrete diffusion model trained only on tile completion, without solvers, rewards, or solvability labels, generates Sokoban puzzles that are solvable 77.4% of the time, and removing a single wall makes 94.5% of the remaining failures solvable. The result shows that a global, search-heavy property can emerge from a purely local masked-cell training objective.",
