          "title": "Aborted but Not Forgotten: KV-Cache Retention Breaks Rollback Consistency in Language Agents",
          "title_zh": "已中止却未被遗忘：KV 缓存保留破坏语言智能体的回滚一致性",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15939v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.15939",
          "summary": "Stateful language agents assume an aborted branch can be discarded by clearing it from the transcript, but retained KV-cache state can let the model keep attending to content the application believes it removed. The authors formalize rollback consistency and show across seven open-weight model families that retained KV alone flips a typed protected effect in 25 of 63 audited cells, while rebuilding the cache closes the channel.",
