          "title": "Adversarial Review: Structured Disagreement for Grounded Agentic Code Review",
          "title_zh": "对抗式评审：面向有据可依的智能体代码评审的结构化分歧",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18167v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.18167",
          "summary": "Adversarial Review is a minimal three-agent code-review protocol pairing a main coding agent with a reviewer and a critic that audits the review through structured disagreement before edits are made. It achieves the highest pass rate on LiveCodeBench, and on SWE-PRBench a single prompt iteration that makes disagreement explicit reaches the highest F1 while avoiding a false-consensus failure mode.",
